# Lab 1.1 — RAID 1 + File Integrity Monitoring

## What this covers
Mirrored storage for redundancy, then Windows audit policy to detect
file changes on that volume.

## Procedure
1. Create two equal-sized virtual disks, leave them unallocated
2. Convert both to dynamic disks
3. Create a mirrored volume across them, format NTFS, label "RAID 1 VOL"
4. Enable Object Access > File System auditing (Success + Failure)
5. Attach a SACL to the target folder via Properties > Security >
   Advanced > Auditing
6. Modify a file in that folder
7. Filter Security log for 4656, 4663, 4660

## Key insight
Audit policy and SACL are two separate switches. Both must be on or
nothing logs. This is the thing that trips people up.

## Event IDs
- 4656 — handle requested
- 4663 — object accessed
- 4660 — object deleted


